  "body_html": "<h1>Convex Games Have Nonempty Core</h1>\n<p><strong>Theorem.</strong> If a finite TU game is convex, then its core is nonempty.</p>",
  "proof_html": "<p>Sketch</p>\n<p>Convexity implies the balancedness inequalities required by\nBondareva-Shapley. Applying\n[[game_theory.coalitional_game.bondareva_shapley]] then gives\nnonemptiness of the core.</p>\n<h2>Lean Status</h2>\n<p>The theorem statement exists as <code>CoalitionalGame.IsConvex.core_nonempty</code>\nand currently has a documented proof gap, depending on the\nBondareva-Shapley proof route.</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[MSZ Ch.17, Thm 17.55] Maschler, Solan, Zamir, <em>Game Theory</em>,\n  <code>references/GameTheory.pdf</code>.</li>\n</ul>",
